--- a/deploy/README.md
+++ b/deploy/README.md
@@ -201,6 +201,38 @@ which could also change the account's email or delete it. The account always com
 token. Guests have nothing to manage: their progress stays in the browser, and a guest result is
 stored only if they typed a name, with no link to anything else.
 
+## levelup on the same accounts
+
+levelup (a second study site) signs in with this user pool through its own app client and syncs
+its study state **from the browser straight to `LevelupSyncTable`**, with one-hour credentials
+from an identity pool. There is no API route, no Lambda and no log for it, and get-certified's
+progress, results and leaderboard are untouched.
+
+- **Isolation.** The role lets a signed-in identity `GetItem`, `PutItem` and `DeleteItem` only the
+  item whose key is its own identity id (`dynamodb:LeadingKeys`), and `PutItem` only with the
+  attributes `id`, `s`, `j`, `u`. Guests get no credentials (`AllowUnauthenticatedIdentities: false`).
+- **Account data.** levelup has its own "delete synced data" (the `DeleteItem` above) and exports
+  its state from the browser. `DELETE /me` here removes the Cognito user but not that item, which
+  is keyed by identity id, not by `sub`.
+- **Off switch.** Deploy with `LevelupOrigin=''` to remove the client, identity pool and role. The
+  table is retained.
+
+**Cost: fixed by the template, not by traffic.** The table is `PROVISIONED` at 5 read and 5 write
+units with no autoscaling, so a request over capacity is throttled, not billed. `check:infra`
+fails the gate if that table ever becomes on-demand, autoscaled or larger than 10 + 10 units.
+
+| Item | Worst case per month |
+|---|---|
+| Capacity, 5 WCU + 5 RCU | $0 inside DynamoDB's always-free 25 WCU + 25 RCU (per account and Region, provisioned tables only; the other tables here are on-demand, so it is unused). Without it: 5 × $0.00065 + 5 × $0.00013 per hour × 730 h ≈ **$2.85** (us-east-1 list price, checked 2026-11-11) |
+| Storage | One item per identity, at most 400 KB (DynamoDB's item limit). Identities come only from verified accounts, and Cognito's default email sender caps verification emails per day (forum reports put it at 50). About 0.6 GB a month at most, inside the 25 GB always-free, then $0.25/GB |
+| Identity pool | No charge (Cognito pricing page) |
+| API Gateway, Lambda, logs | None used |
+
+So the worst case is **$0 with the always-free tier and under $3 without it**, whatever a caller
+does. The price of the bound: under a flood, sync slows for everyone (throttled), while each
+browser keeps working on its local copy and retries later. MAUs from levelup sign-ins count
+toward the user pool's free monthly active users like any other sign-in.
+
 ## Testimonials
 
 Learners' stories at `#/testimonials`, on the home page and on each cert's landing page.
